# Code Validation & Quality Enforcement

---
description: Automated checks and validations for code quality
alwaysApply: true
---

## Automatic Validations

Perform these checks on every code generation/modification:

### 1. i18n Compliance Detection
```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Any hardcoded UI text
<Button>Save</Button>
<div>Error loading data</div>
<input aria-label="Email address" />
<form aria-describedby="Login form" />

// ✅ REQUIRED - All text through useTranslation
const { t } = useTranslation(['featureName', 'common']);
<Button>{t('button.save')}</Button>
<div>{t('error.loadFailed')}</div>
<input aria-label={t('a11y.emailInput')} />
<form aria-describedby={t('a11y.loginForm')} />
```

**Auto-fix Strategy**:
1. Replace hardcoded strings with `t('suggested.key')`
2. Add key to appropriate namespace file:
   - Feature text → `src/features/{feature}/locales/{lang}/{namespace}.json`
   - Global text → `src/locales/{lang}/common.json`
   - ARIA labels → under `a11y` section
3. Check if namespace is registered in `src/locales/i18n.ts`

### 2. Design System Enforcement
```typescript
// ❌ AVOID
<button className="bg-blue-500 px-4 py-2">Click me</button>
<div className="flex items-center">...</div>

// ✅ PREFER
<Button variant="primary">Click me</Button>
<Container layout="flex-center">...</Container>
```

**Auto-suggestion**: When detecting raw HTML + Tailwind, suggest design system alternative

### 3. Feature Structure Validation
Check that files are in correct directories:
- React hooks → `hooks/` directory
- API functions → `api/` directory  
- Type definitions → `types/` directory
- Page components → `pages/` directory

### 4. Duplicate Prevention
Before creating new files, scan for:
- Existing components with same name
- Similar hooks or utilities
- Duplicate route paths
- Existing API modules for same endpoint

### 5. Language Compliance
Detect non-English identifiers:
```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN
const benutzerName = "John";
const fetchBenutzerDaten = () => {};

// ✅ REQUIRED
const userName = "John";
const fetchUserData = () => {};
```

### 6. Layout Enforcement
Every page component must use layout wrapper:
```typescript
// ❌ MISSING LAYOUT
export const UserPage = () => {
  return <div>Content</div>;
};

// ✅ CORRECT
export const UserPage = () => {
  return (
    <MainLayout>
      <div>Content</div>
    </MainLayout>
  );
};
```

### 7. API Pattern Validation
Ensure proper API structure:
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Multiple endpoints in one file
export const userService = {
  getUsers: () => fetch('/users'),
  createUser: () => fetch('/users', {method: 'POST'}),
  deleteUser: () => fetch('/users/1', {method: 'DELETE'})
};

// ✅ CORRECT - One file per endpoint
// api/fetchUsers.ts
export const fetchUsers = () => axiosInstance.get('/users');

// api/createUser.ts  
export const createUser = (data) => axiosInstance.post('/users', data);
```

## Error Messages & Suggestions

When validation fails, provide specific guidance:
- "Hardcoded string detected in JSX. Use t('suggested.key') instead and add to {namespace}.json"
- "ARIA label not localized. Move to a11y section: t('a11y.suggested')"  
- "Raw button element found. Use <Button> from design system"
- "Hook placed in wrong directory. Move to features/[name]/hooks/"
- "Translation namespace 'users' not registered in i18n.ts"
- "Missing translation file: src/features/{feature}/locales/de/{namespace}.json"
- "Component name uses German. Suggest English alternative: {suggestion}"

## Integration Points

Validate integration between features:
- Check route uniqueness across all features
- Verify type imports use proper feature exports
- Ensure shared components come from design system
- Confirm API calls use centralized axios instance with auth headers
- Validate i18n namespace registration and file structure consistency

### 8. i18n Structure Validation
Ensure proper internationalization setup:
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Missing namespace registration
// Component uses 'users' namespace but it's not in i18n.ts

// ❌ WRONG - Hardcoded ARIA labels
<button aria-label="Save changes">Save</button>

// ❌ WRONG - Mixed hardcoded and localized text
<div>Welcome {t('user.name')}!</div>

// ✅ CORRECT - Proper namespace usage
const { t } = useTranslation(['users', 'common']);
<button aria-label={t('a11y.saveButton')}>{t('button.save')}</button>

// ✅ CORRECT - Parameterized translations
<div>{t('welcome.message', { name: user.name })}</div>
```

**File Structure Checks**:
- Verify translation files exist in both `de/` and `en/` subdirectories
- Check that namespaces are registered in `src/locales/i18n.ts`
- Ensure `a11y` section exists for accessibility labels
- Validate JSON structure consistency across languages